-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CCFULL-ROM prediction input (python -m emulator.run_rom).  The lines are read
in order; blank lines and lines starting with # are skipped, and nothing after
the dashed line is read.  Paths are relative to the project root.  The trained
parameter box, energy range, and experimental data come from the model.

 1   name of the trained model, global or local, e.g.
     34S_168Er_Local_Channel7_Snap300_POD80_EIM48.
 2   folder of the trained models (line 12 of emulator_train.in).
 3   basis rank: 0 uses the trained rank.  A smaller rank keeps the leading
     POD vectors and gives the same result as a training at that rank.  For a
     local model it is the rank per (E, J).
 4   points: single (line 5), latin_hypercube (line 6), or table (line 7).
 5   single point: beta2,beta4,beta6,V0,r0,a0.  It may lie outside the box.
 6   Latin hypercube: number of points, seed.
 7   table of points: a CSV file with a header line and the columns
     beta2,beta4,beta6,v0,r0,a0 in this order.
 8   box of the Latin hypercube: training (the box of the model), or custom
     (lines 9-10), which may extend beyond it.
 9   custom bounds of beta2, beta4, beta6, as line 13 of emulator_train.in.
 10  custom bounds of V0, r0, a0, as line 14 of emulator_train.in.
 11  energies: experimental (the measured energies of the model's data), grid
     (line 12), or selected (line 13).  They must lie in the trained range;
     a local model emulates only the energies it was built for.
 12  energy grid: first, last, step in MeV.
 13  selected energies in MeV; keep a value here even when it is not used.
 14  1 = yes, 0 = no: show the measured cross sections; check against the
     exact CCFULL program (physical_model/ccfull_clean) at the same points and
     energies; report exact time / ROM time (needs the check).
 15  output directory; every run writes a new timestamped directory in it.
 16  1 = yes, 0 = no: write cross_sections.csv, run_summary.json, and
     point_timings.csv (ROM and exact time of every point).
